idth: 50.303%"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding: 0; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-size: 10pt; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; text-decoration: none; font-family: Arial; vertical-align: bottom; white-space: nowrap; width: 7.75758%"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding: 0; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-size: 10pt; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; text-decoration: none; font-family: Arial; vertical-align: bottom; white-space: nowrap; width: 7.63636%"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;</ferc:StatementAboutImportantChangesDuringTheQuarterYearTextBlock>
    <ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="f-2494" contextRef="c-21">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;NOTE A - ORGANIZATION AND OPERATIONS:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Organization.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Gulf Run Transmission, LLC (&amp;quot;Gulf Run&amp;quot;), a Delaware limited liability company, is an indirect wholly-owned subsidiary of Energy Transfer LP (&amp;quot;Energy Transfer&amp;quot;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; text-align: justify"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Operations.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Gulf Run&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt; &lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;is&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt; &lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;primarily engaged in the interstate transportation of natural gas and as such, Gulf Run is subject to the jurisdiction of the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (&amp;quot;FERC&amp;quot;). Gulf Run owns approximately 335 miles of natural gas pipeline, which includes approximately 200 miles of pipeline transferred from Enable Gas Transmission, LLC (&amp;quot;EGT&amp;quot;), an indirect subsidiary of Energy Transfer, designed to transport 3.0 billion cubic feet per day. Gulf Run, placed in service in December 2022, is a large diameter pipeline that runs from the heart of the Haynesville Shale in East Texas and North Louisiana to the Carthage and Perryville natural gas hubs and other key markets along the Gulf Coast.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt; &lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Gulf Run evaluated subsequent events through &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)"&gt;April 10, 2026&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;, the date on which these accompanying financial statements were available to be issued. Any material subsequent events that occurred during this time have been properly recognized and/or disclosed in these financial statements. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; text-indent: 22.5pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;NOTE B - ESTIMATES AND SIGNIFICANT ACCOUNTING POLICIES:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-top: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt;&lt;b style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; background-color: unset; text-align: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration-line: underline"&gt;1. Basis of Presentation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Gulf Run's financial statements have been prepared in accordance with the accounting requirements of the FERC, as set forth in the applicable Uniform System of Accounts and published accounting releases, which constitute a comprehensive basis of accounting other than accounting principles generally accepted in the United States of America (&amp;quot;GAAP&amp;quot;). The most significant differences between GAAP and the financial statements presented herein are: (1) classification of certain accounts on the balance sheet, statement of income and statement of cash flows, (2) certain assets and liabilities that result from the regulated ratemaking process are recorded that would not be recorded under GAAP for non-regulated entities.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-top: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt;&lt;b style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; background-color: unset; text-align: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration-line: underline"&gt;2. Use of Estimates&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; text-indent: 22.5pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;The preparation of financial statements requires management to make estimates and assumptions that affect the reported amounts of assets and liabilities and the accrual for and disclosure of contingent assets and liabilities at the date of the financial statements and the reported amounts of revenues and expenses during the reporting period. Although these estimates are based on management's available knowledge of current and expected future events, actual results could differ from those estimates.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-top: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; background-color: unset; text-align: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-weight: bold; text-decoration-line: underline"&gt;3. Cash and Cash Equivalents&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Gulf Run has a cash management agreement with Energy Transfer which authorizes Energy Transfer or its designated affiliate to provide cash management services to Gulf Run. At the close of each business day, the agreement allows for Gulf Run to transfer funds in excess of general operating purposes to Energy Transfer or if Gulf Run has insufficient funds to meet its general operating purposes, Energy Transfer will transfer all funds necessary to Gulf Run.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-top: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt;&lt;b style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; background-color: unset; text-align: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration-line: underline"&gt;4. Plant Materials and Operating Supplies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Plant materials and operating supplies are carried at the lower of weighted average cost or net realizable value. Materials transferred out of warehouses are priced at weighted average cost.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-top: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt;&lt;b style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; background-color: unset; text-align: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration-line: underline"&gt;5. Natural Gas Imbalances&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Natural gas imbalances occur as a result of differences in volumes of natural gas received and delivered. Gulf Run values natural gas imbalance receivables and payables at current market price. Natural gas imbalances are generally settled in cash or made up in-kind subject to the terms of Gulf Run's tariff with no impact on revenues.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-top: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt;&lt;b style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; background-color: unset; text-align: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration-line: underline"&gt;6. System Balancing Gas&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Gas held for transmission operations is recorded in System balancing gas, Account 117.2, using the fixed asset accounting model established under FERC's order No. 581. Under this approach, system balancing gas is valued at historical cost. Periodically, unbalanced transactions from exchange imbalances or load balancing transactions may create a liability position for system balancing gas and is recorded in Gas owed to system gas, Account 117.4.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;b style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; background-color: unset; text-align: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration-line: underline"&gt;7. Gas Owed to System Gas&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;b style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; background-color: unset; text-align: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration-line: underline"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Gulf Run accounts for Gas owed to system gas, Account 117.4, using the fixed asset accounting model established under FERC's order No. 581. Under this approach, gas owed to system gas volumes are classified as fixed assets and valued at historical cost. Encroachments upon gas owed to system gas are valued at current market prices. Gulf Run may sell gas owed to system gas in excess of its system operational requirements.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;b style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; background-color: unset; text-align: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration-line: underline"&gt;8. Fuel Tracker&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.5in"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Gulf Run has a fuel tracker mechanism whereby it recovers gas used and lost on its system via in-kind receipts of volumes from its shippers. The fuel tracker mechanism for Gulf Run has a true-up provision that any over/under recoveries of volumes are returned to or collected from shippers through prospective annual adjustments to the fuel retention rates. A regulatory asset or regulatory liability is established for the difference between the volumes collected and the volumes actually used/lost in the system. The net over/under recovered volumes are valued at current market prices in Other regulatory assets, Account 182.3, or Other regulatory liabilities, Account 254, as applicable. As of December 31, 2025 and 2024, Gulf Run's fuel tracker has a balance of $1.3 million and $1.7 million in Other regulatory liabilities, Account 254, respectively.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-top: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt;&lt;b style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; background-color: unset; text-align: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration-line: underline"&gt;9. Utility Plant&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;i&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Additions.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Ongoing additions of utility plant are stated at original cost. Gulf Run capitalizes all construction-related direct labor and material costs, as well as indirect construction costs. Such indirect construction costs primarily include labor and related costs of departments associated with supporting construction activities and allowance for funds used during construction. The indirect capitalized labor and related costs are largely based upon results of periodic time studies or management reviews of time allocations, which provide an estimate of time spent supporting construction projects. The cost of replacements and betterments that extend the useful life of utility plant is also capitalized. The cost of repairs and replacements of minor utility plant items is charged to expense as incurred.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;i&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Retirements.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;When ordinary retirements of utility plant occur, the original cost plus cost of removal less salvage value is removed by a charge to accumulated depreciation and amortization, with no gain or loss recorded. When entire regulated operating units of utility plant are sold, the original cost and related accumulated depreciation and amortization accounts are removed, with any resulting gain or loss recorded in the statement of income.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;i&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Depreciation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Gulf Run computed depreciation expense under the composite method using FERC-approved depreciation rates. For general and intangible plant, Gulf Run computed depreciation expense under the straight-line method using FERC-approved depreciation rates.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;i&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Allowance for Funds Used During Construction.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Gulf Run capitalizes the cost of funds used during construction for capital projects. The rates used by Gulf Run are calculated pursuant to the FERC rules, which include an allowance for the cost of debt and equity funds.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-top: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt;&lt;b style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; background-color: unset; text-align: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration-line: underline"&gt;10. Asset Retirement Obligation (&amp;quot;ARO&amp;quot;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.5in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Legal obligations associated with the retirement of long-lived assets are recorded at fair value at the time the obligations are incurred, if a reasonable estimate of fair value can be made. Present value techniques are used which reflect assumptions such as removal and remediation costs, inflation, and profit margins that third parties would demand to settle the amount of the future obligation. Gulf Run did not include a market risk premium for unforeseeable circumstances in its fair value estimates because such a premium could not be reasonably estimated. Upon initial recognition of the liability, costs are capitalized as part of the long-lived asset and depreciated over the useful life of the related asset. The liability is accreted to its present value each period with accretion being recorded to operating expense or regulatory asset, as applicable, with a corresponding increase in the carrying amount of the liability. Gulf Run was not able to reasonably measure the fair value of the AROs as of December 31, 2025 or 2024 as the expected settlement dates were indeterminable. Gulf Run will record an ARO in the periods in which Gulf Run can reasonably determine the settlement dates.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-top: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt;&lt;b style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; background-color: unset; text-align: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration-line: underline"&gt;11. Related Party Transactions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Related party transactions primarily include revenues earned from and payments for services provided by Energy Transfer and its subsidiaries. Transactions are generally allocated based on relevant criteria, including time spent, utility plant, gross margin, salaries, or other appropriate methods.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-top: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt;&lt;b style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; background-color: unset; text-align: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration-line: underline"&gt;12. Environmental Expenditures&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Environmental expenditures that relate to an existing condition caused by past operations that do not contribute to current or future revenue generation are expensed. Environmental expenditures relating to current or future revenues are expensed or capitalized as appropriate. Liabilities are recorded when environmental assessments and/or clean-ups are probable and the costs can be reasonably estimated. Remediation obligations are not discounted because the timing of future cash flow streams is not predictable. As of December 31, 2025 and 2024, there were no amounts accrued for future environmental expenditures.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;b style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; background-color: unset; text-align: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration-line: underline"&gt;13. Revenue Recognition&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Gulf Run's revenues from transportation of natural gas are based on capacity reservation charges and, to a lesser extent, commodity usage charges. Reservation revenues, recognized monthly, are based on contracted rates and capacity reserved by the customers. Revenues from commodity usage charges, also recognized monthly, are based on the volumes received from or delivered to the customer, based on Gulf Run's tariff. Revenues collected during the pendency of a rate proceeding may be required by the FERC to be refunded in the final order. Gulf Run establishes reserves for such potential refunds, as appropriate. No such reserves were required as of December 31, 2025 and 2024.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;b style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; background-color: unset; text-align: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration-line: underline"&gt;14. Accounts Receivable and Allowance for Expected Credit Losses&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Gulf Run has customers in the energy segment that may impact Gulf Run's overall exposure to credit risk, either positively or negatively, in that the customers may be similarly affected by changes in economic or other conditions. Gulf Run manages trade credit risk to mitigate credit losses and exposure to uncollectible trade receivables. Prospective and existing customers are reviewed regularly for creditworthiness based upon pre-established standards consistent with FERC filed tariffs to manage credit risk within approved tolerances. Customers that do not meet minimum credit standards are required to provide additional credit support in the form of a letter of credit, prepayment, or other forms of security. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Gulf Run establishes an allowance for expected credit losses on trade receivables based on the expected ultimate recovery of these receivables and considers many factors including historical customer collection experience, general and specific economic trends and known specific issues related to individual customers, sectors, and transactions that might impact collectability. Changes in the allowance are recorded as a component of operating expenses; reductions in the allowance are recorded when receivables are subsequently collected or written-off. Past-due receivable balances are written-off when Gulf Run's efforts have been unsuccessful in collecting the amount due. Gulf Run's allowance for expected credit losses was not material as of December 31, 2025 and 2024.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;The following table presents the relative contribution to Gulf Run's total transportation revenues from operations of each customer that comprised at least 10% of its revenues:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p align="center" style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in; text-align: center"&gt;&lt;img src="data:image/png;base64," class="e-rte-image e-imginline" width="auto" height="auto" style="min-width: 0; max-width: 1752px; min-height: 0" alt="" /&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; margin-left: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Gulf Run has the following transportation receivables from these customers at the dates indicated: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p align="center" style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in; text-align: center"&gt;&lt;img src="data:image/png;base64," class="e-rte-image e-imginline" width="auto" height="auto" style="min-width: 0; max-width: 1752px; min-height: 0" alt="" /&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in; text-align: center"&gt; &lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;In addition to the concentration of revenue risk by customers discussed above, Gulf Run has a customer with outstanding accounts receivable greater than 10% from all customers. This customer has transportation receivable of $3.0 million and $1.5 million as of December 31, 2025 and 2024, respectively.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-top: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt;&lt;b style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; background-color: unset; text-align: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration-line: underline"&gt;15. Fair Value Measurement&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;The carrying amounts of accounts receivable and accounts payable approximate their fair value.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-top: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt;&lt;b style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; text-align: justify; background-color: unset"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration-line: underline"&gt;16. Income Taxes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;The FERC's Revised Policy Statement on Treatment of Income Taxes, Docket No. PL17-1, states that it no longer permits master limited partnerships including a company that does not pay taxes itself and is owned by a master limited partnership, to recover an income tax allowance in their cost of service.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-top: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt;&lt;b style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; background-color: unset; text-align: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration-line: underline"&gt;17. Taxes, Other Than on Income&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Taxes, other than on income primarily consist of ad valorem tax paid on the assessed value of Gulf Run's natural gas transmission lines based on fixed rates established by the applicable state or local taxing authorities. Ad valorem taxes are generally based on assessed property value at the beginning of each year.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-top: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt;&lt;b style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; background-color: unset; text-align: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration-line: underline"&gt;18. Commitments and Contingencies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Gulf Run is subject to proceedings, lawsuits and other claims related to environmental and other matters. Accounting for contingencies requires significant judgment by management regarding the estimated probabilities and ranges of exposure to potential liability.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;NOTE C - RELATED PARTY TRANSACTIONS:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;The following table provides a summary of the associated transactions for the periods presented:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p align="center" style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in; text-align: center"&gt;&lt;img src="data:image/png;base64," class="e-rte-image e-imginline" width="auto" height="auto" style="min-width: 0; max-width: 1752px; min-height: 0" alt="" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in; text-align: left"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; background-color: unset"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in; text-align: left"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; background-color: unset"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; text-align: inherit; background-color: unset; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;     (1) Transportation and operational sales related revenues primarily from EGT and Trunkline Gas Company, LLC (&amp;quot;TGC&amp;quot;), indirect wholly-owned subsidiaries of Energy Transfer.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in; text-align: left"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; text-align: inherit; background-color: unset; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;     (2) C&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; background-color: unset; text-align: inherit"&gt;orporate charges and services provided by Energy Transfer and its subsidiaries.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in; text-align: left"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; background-color: unset; text-align: inherit"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;     (3) Transportation and compression expenses purchased from E&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; background-color: unset; text-align: inherit"&gt;GT and TGC.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.25in; font-size: 11pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Garamond&amp;quot;, serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 11pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Garamond&amp;quot;, serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.25in; font-size: 11pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Garamond&amp;quot;, serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Accounts receivable from and accounts payable to associated companies are primarily related to the cash management activity, transportation of natural gas and various operating and administrative services provided by Energy Transfer and its subsidiaries.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.25in; font-size: 11pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Garamond&amp;quot;, serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.25in; font-size: 11pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Garamond&amp;quot;, serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Gulf Run leases natural gas capacity of up to 445,000 dekatherms per day on its Line CP, Docket Nos. CP20-68-000, CP20-70-000, to EGT. The term of the capacity lease agreement extends until December 31, 2027 and thereafter the term is year to year.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 11pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Garamond&amp;quot;, serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.25in; font-size: 11pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Garamond&amp;quot;, serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Gulf Run has transportation and exchange gas receivables and payables with associated companies as a result of differences in volumes of gas received and delivered for those associated companies. The imbalances are settled based on the operator balancing agreements that Gulf Run has with those associated companies.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.25in; font-size: 11pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Garamond&amp;quot;, serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.25in; font-size: 11pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Garamond&amp;quot;, serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;The following table sets forth the balances with associated companies within transportation and exchange gas receivables and payables reflected in Miscellaneous current and accrued assets, Account 174, and Miscellaneous current and accrued liabilities, Account 242, respectively, on the balance sheet:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.25in; font-size: 11pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Garamond&amp;quot;, serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 0 0.25in; font-size: 11pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Garamond&amp;quot;, serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p align="center" style="margin: 0 0 12pt 0.25in; font-size: 11pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Garamond&amp;quot;, serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-align: center"&gt;&lt;img src="data:image/png;base64," class="e-rte-image e-imginline" width="auto" height="auto" alt="" style="vertical-align: bottom; border: 0; cursor: pointer; display: inline-block; float: none; margin: auto 5px; max-width: 1752px; position: relative; padding: 1px; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; font-size: 16px; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: center; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); min-width: 0; min-height: 0" /&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; margin-left: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;NOTE D - UTILITY PLANT:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; margin-left: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;The following table provides a summary of utility plant at the dates indicated.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p align="center" style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin: 0 0 0 0.25in; text-align: center"&gt;&lt;img src="data:image/png;base64," class="e-rte-image e-imginline" width="auto" height="auto" style="min-width: 0; max-width: 1752px; min-height: 0" alt="" /&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; margin-left: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; margin-left: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;NOTE E - COMMITMENTS, CONTINGENCIES AND ENVIRONMENTAL LIABILITIES:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; margin-left: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Williams Antitrust Litigation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt; On June 28, 2024, Louisiana Energy Gateway LLC, The Williams Companies, Inc., and Williams Fields Services Group, LLC (collectively, &amp;quot;Williams&amp;quot;) filed a Petition for Damages against Energy Transfer and Gulf Run in the 42nd Judicial District Court, Parish of DeSoto, State of Louisiana (&amp;quot;District Court&amp;quot;), alleging that Energy Transfer and/or Gulf Run have monopolized, conspired to monopolize and/or attempted to monopolize, the relevant product and geographic market for the movement of natural gas from the Haynesville Shale in northwestern Louisiana south to natural gas facilities in the Louisiana Gulf Coast (the &amp;quot;Relevant Market&amp;quot;), engaged in acquisitions that have directly enabled and incentivized to substantially lessen competition, and engaged in unfair methods of competition and unfair trade practices.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;On September 16, 2024, Energy Transfer and Gulf Run removed the case to the United States District Court for the Western District of Louisiana (&amp;quot;Federal Court&amp;quot;). On October 4, 2024, Williams filed a Motion to Remand with the Federal Court, seeking to remand the case back to the District Court. On October 21, 2024, Energy Transfer and Gulf Run filed a consent to remand based on a subsequent change in circumstances. After the case was remanded, on November 18, 2024, Energy Transfer and Gulf Run filed a Peremptory Exception of No Cause, asserting that Williams failed to state a cause of action. The Peremptory Exception was heard on February 10, 2025 and denied. The District Court initially set the case for trial on September 14, 2026, but indicated that trial will be continued to 2027. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; margin-left: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Liabilities for Litigation and Other Claims.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Gulf Run records accrued liabilities for litigation and other claim costs when management believes a loss is probable and reasonably estimable. When management believes there is at least a reasonable possibility that a material loss or an additional material loss may have been incurred, Gulf Run discloses (i) an estimate of the possible loss or range of loss in excess of the amount accrued; or (ii) a statement that such an estimate cannot be made. As of December 31, 2025 and 2024, Gulf Run had no recorded litigation or other claim-related accrued liabilities. Gulf Run does not have any material litigation or other claim contingency other than the items documented in the proceeding above.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Environmental Matters.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Gulf Run's operations are subject to extensive federal,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;state and local environmental and safety laws and regulations that require expenditures to ensure compliance, including related to air emissions and wastewater discharges, at operating facilities and for remediation at current and former facilities as well as waste disposal sites. Historically, Gulf Run's environmental compliance costs have not had a material adverse effect on its results of operations but there can be no assurance that such costs will not be material in the future or that such future compliance with existing, amended or new legal requirements will not have a material adverse effect on Gulf Run's business and operating results. Costs of planning, designing, constructing and operating pipelines and other facilities must incorporate compliance with environmental laws and regulations and safety standards. Failure to comply with these laws and regulations may result in the assessment of administrative, civil and criminal penalties, the imposition of investigatory, remedial and corrective action obligations, natural resource damages, the issuance of injunctions in affected areas and the filing of federally authorized citizen suits. Contingent losses related to all significant known environmental matters have been accrued and/or separately disclosed. However, Gulf Run may revise accrual amounts prior to resolution of a particular contingency based on changes in facts and circumstances or changes in the expected outcome.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Environmental exposures and liabilities are difficult to assess and estimate due to unknown factors such as the magnitude of possible contamination, the timing and extent of remediation, the determination of Gulf Run's liability in proportion to other parties, improvements in cleanup technologies and the extent to which environmental laws and regulations may change in the future. Although environmental&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;costs may have a significant impact on Gulf Run's results of operations for any single period, Gulf Run believes that such costs will not have a material adverse effect on its financial position. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; margin-left: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Air Quality Standards.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;In 2023,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt; &lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;the United States Environmental Protection Agency (&amp;quot;EPA&amp;quot;) finalized its Good Neighbor Plan (the &amp;quot;Plan&amp;quot;) which seeks to reduce nitrogen oxide pollution from power plants and other industrial facilities from 23 upwind states which the EPA determined is contributing to National Ambient Air Quality Standards (&amp;quot;NAAQS&amp;quot;) nonattainment and interfering with maintenance of the 2015 ozone NAAQS in downwind states. As part of the Plan, the EPA announced that it would be issuing prescriptive emission standards for several sectors, including certain new and existing internal combustion engines of a certain size used in pipeline transportation of natural gas. The EPA's final rule was to become effective on August 4, 2023, and the prescribed emission standards were scheduled to be effective in 2026. However, on March 12, 2025, the EPA announced plans to end the Plan. Operators and industry groups have challenged the Plan in the District of Columbia Circuit (&amp;quot;D.C. Circuit&amp;quot;), as well as the legal predicates to individual upwind states' inclusion in the Plan in the regional circuits. The effectiveness of the rule is currently stayed in certain states within Energy Transfer's footprint, by nature of judicial stays of the legal predicate to the Plan, by judicial stay of the Plan itself by the United States Supreme Court (&amp;quot;U.S. Supreme Court&amp;quot;), or by the administrative stay issued by the EPA in October 2024. On June 18,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;2025, the U.S. Supreme Court ruled that the regional circuits are the appropriate venue for the proceedings. On July 30, 2025, the United States Court of Appeals for the Tenth Circuit placed the case in abeyance pending the EPA's reconsideration of its disapproval of upwind states' state implementation plans addressing their Plan obligations. Proceedings challenging the Plan in the D.C. Circuit were also placed in abeyance on May 2, 2025 pending the EPA's reconsideration of the Plan. The EPA is preparing a proposed rulemaking as part of the reconsideration process, and on January 27, 2026, the EPA announced its proposal to approve state implementation plans for certain states, including those in which Gulf Run operates, which would resolve those states' obligations under the Good Neighbor Plan. Gulf Run cannot predict with any certainty the substance of any later proposed rule or the potential impacts on Gulf Run. Gulf Run currently estimates that the existing final rule would require retrofitting or replacement of certain of its engines used in its operations. Compliance with the Plan (if implementation is not stayed or otherwise delayed) may require substantial capital expenditures which could adversely affect Gulf Run's business in future periods. However, at this time, Gulf Run is still assessing the potential costs of this rule and, given uncertainties resulting from the multiple legal challenges filed against the Plan in various states, in the D.C. Circuit and the U.S. Supreme Court, Gulf Run cannot predict with any certainty what the final costs of compliance for the Plan for Gulf Run ultimately may be.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Other Commitments and Contingencies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Federal Pipeline Integrity Rules.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Gulf Run's pipeline operations are subject to regulation by the United States Department of Transportation under the Pipeline Hazardous Materials Safety Administration (&amp;quot;PHMSA&amp;quot;), pursuant to which PHMSA has established requirements relating to the design, installation, testing, construction, operation, replacement and management of pipeline facilities.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Moreover, PHMSA, through the Office of Pipeline Safety, has promulgated a rule requiring pipeline operators to develop integrity management programs to comprehensively evaluate their pipelines, and take measures to protect pipeline segments located in what the rule refers to as &amp;quot;high consequence areas&amp;quot;. Activities under these integrity management programs involve the performance of internal pipeline inspections, pressure testing or other effective means to assess the integrity of these regulated pipeline segments, and the regulations require prompt action to address integrity issues raised by the assessment and analysis. Integrity testing and assessment of all of these assets will continue, and the results of such testing and assessment could cause Gulf Run to incur future capital and operating expenditures for repairs or upgrades deemed necessary to ensure the continued safe and reliable operation of Gulf Run; however, no estimate can be made at this time of the likely range of such expenditures.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Gulf Run's operations are also subject to the requirements of the Federal Occupational Safety and Health Act (&amp;quot;OSHA&amp;quot;), and comparable state laws that regulate the protection of the health and safety of employees. In addition, the Occupational Safety and Health Administration's hazardous communication standard requires that information be maintained about hazardous materials used or produced in Gulf Run's operations and that this information be provided to employees, state and local government authorities and citizens. Gulf Run believes that its past costs for OSHA required activities, including general industry standards, record keeping requirements and monitoring of occupational exposure to regulated substances have not had a material adverse effect on Gulf Run's results of operations; however, there is no assurance that such costs will not be material in the future.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;NOTE F - REVENUE:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Contract Balances with Customers. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Gulf Run satisfies its obligations by transferring goods or services in exchange for consideration from customers. The timing of performance may differ from the timing the associated consideration is paid to or received from the customer, thus resulting in the recognition of a contract asset or a contract liability. As of January 1, 2024, the opening balance of accounts receivable from contracts with customers was $15.5 million.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Gulf Run recognizes a contract asset when making upfront consideration payments to certain customers or when providing services to customers prior to the time at which Gulf Run is contractually allowed to bill for such services. As of December 31, 2025 and 2024, no contract assets have been recognized.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Gulf Run recognizes a contract liability if the customer's payment of consideration precedes Gulf Run's fulfillment of the performance obligations. As of December 31, 2025 and 2024, no contract liabilities have been recognized.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Performance Obligation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;At contract inception, Gulf Run assesses the goods and services promised in its contracts with customers and identifies a performance obligation for each promise to transfer a good or service (or bundle of goods or services) that is distinct. To identify the performance obligations, Gulf Run considers all the goods or services promised in the contract, whether explicitly stated or implied based on customary business practices. For a contract that has more than one performance obligation, Gulf Run allocates the total contract consideration it expects to be entitled to, to each distinct performance obligation based on a standalone-selling price basis. Revenue is recognized when (or as) the performance obligations are satisfied, that is, when the customer obtains control of the good or service. Certain of Gulf Run's contracts contain variable components, which, when combined with the fixed component are considered a single performance obligation. For these types of contracts, only the fixed component of the contracts are included in the amount of revenue expected to be recognized on contracts with customers existing as of December 31, 2025.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;As of December 31, 2025, the aggregate amounts of transaction price allocated to unsatisfied (or partially satisfied) performance obligations is approximately $0.4 billion from 2026 through 2028 and $1.3 billion thereafter that Gulf Run expects to recognize as revenue.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Practical Expedients Utilized by Gulf Run.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Gulf Run elected the following practical expedients in accordance with Accounting Standards Codification Topic 606:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.45in"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Right to invoice&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt; - Gulf Run elected to utilize an output method to recognize revenue that is based on the amount to which Gulf Run has a right to invoice a customer for services performed to date, if that amount corresponds directly with the value provided to the customer for the related performance or its obligation completed to date. As such, Gulf Run recognized revenue in the amount to which it had the right to invoice customers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.45in"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Significant financing component&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt; - Gulf Run elected not to adjust the promised amount of consideration for the effects of significant financing component if Gulf Run expects, at contract inception, that the period between the transfer of a promised good or service to a customer and when the customer pays for that good or service will be one year or less.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.25in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.45in"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Unearned variable consideration&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt; - Gulf Run elected to only disclose the unearned fixed consideration associated with unsatisfied performance obligations related to Gulf Run's various customer contracts which contain both fixed and variable components.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.45in"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;NOTE G - &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;SUPPLEMENTAL CASH FLOW INFORMATION:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-right: 0; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, serif; margin-left: 0.4in"&gt;&lt;img src="data:image/png;base64," class="e-rte-image e-imginline" width="auto" height="auto" style="min-width: 0; max-width: 1752px; min-height: 0" alt="" /&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
